<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Brandenburg-Ansbach</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1398–1806</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Margraviate of Brandenburg-Ansbach, Principality of Ansbach</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Brandenburg-Ansbach was a principality of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franconia">Franconia</a>, ruled by a branch of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-hohenzollern">Hohenzollerns</a> from its capital at Ansbach. It emerged from the Franconian lands of the burgraves of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nuremberg">Nuremberg</a>, divided in 1398, and was held as a margraviate by princes of the family from the 15th century. In 1791 the last margrave, Charles Alexander, ceded it to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>, and in 1806 it passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/brandenburg-ansbach.jpg" alt="Brandenburg-Ansbach" width="320" height="224" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mikmaq · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Principality_of_Ansbach_1791.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
